  "Name": "Raut2011-MgF2-QW-on-BK7",
  "Source": "H. K. Raut, V. A. Ganesh, A. S. Nair, and S. Ramakrishna, \"Anti-reflective coatings: A critical, in-depth review,\" Energy Environ. Sci. 4, 3779-3804 (2011). doi:10.1039/c1ee01297e - Sec. 6.2.1, p. 3783 (text: BK7 n = 1.5151 at 633 nm, MgF2 n = 1.38, reflectance from about 4 % to less than 1.3 % at the centre wavelength, normal incidence); curve in Fig. 7(a), p. 3784",
  "Notes": "Classic single-layer quarter-wave MgF2 AR coating on BK7 glass\nSpecification: Single quarter-wave layer; zero reflectance would need n = sqrt(1.5151) = 1.22 (p. 3783).\nReported: Single-surface reflectance at the centre wavelength, normal incidence: bare BK7 about 4 %, with the MgF2 layer less than 1.3 % (p. 3783, Sec. 6.2.1; with these constant indices R(min) = ((1.5151 - 1.38^2)/(1.5151 + 1.38^2))^2 = 1.30 %). Fig. 7(a) (from ref. 161, not necessarily this exact case) shows the single-layer MgF2 curve with a broad minimum of roughly 1.3 % near 550 nm over 400-700 nm. Single-layer ARCs are said to suppress reflectance to about 2.5 % over 450-1100 nm (p. 3783, ref. 159).\nNotes: The review does not state the centre wavelength; reference_nm = 550 nm is assumed from the position of the minimum in Fig. 7(a). With constant indices the minimum value (1.30 %) does not depend on that choice. Indices are constants: BK7 1.5151 is quoted at 633 nm. Back surface of the glass not included (single interface).\nLayers from Sec. 6.2.1, p. 3783 (text: BK7 n = 1.5151 at 633 nm, MgF2 n = 1.38, reflectance from about 4 % to less than 1.3 % at the centre wavelength, normal incidence); curve in Fig. 7(a), p. 3784; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R min 1.30 % at 550 nm; paper R < 1.3 % at the centre wavelength.",
